%N A239753 Number of pairs of functions (f,g) on a set of n elements into itself satisfying f(x) = g(f(g(x))).
%H A239753 Max Alekseyev, <a href="/A239753/b239753.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A239753 Max A. Alekseyev, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.08674">Counting Finite Maps through Functional Digraphs and Fibers</a>, arXiv:2611.08674 [math.CO], 2026. See pp. 2, 3, 19.
%F A239753 a(n) <= n^2n. - _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Mar 26 2014
%F A239753 For n > 0, a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} binomial(n-1,k-1) * k! * n^(n-k) * A001372(k). - _Max Alekseyev_, Nov 14 2026
